.TH TUI_HISTVIEW_INIT 3 2026-10-21 "libtuikit 0.11" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_histview_init, tui_histview_free, tui_histview_set_rows,
tui_histview_set_failed, tui_histview_selected, tui_histview_notice,
tui_histview_modal, tui_histview_handle,
tui_histview_render \- the history view: recorded steps with a Revert entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/histview.h>
.PP
.B typedef struct tui_histview_row {
.B "    uint64_t id;  const char *time, *who, *operation, *object, *thing,"
.B "                  *old_value, *new_value;"
.B "    uint64_t reverts;  int revertable;"
.B } tui_histview_row;
.PP
.BI "typedef int (*tui_histview_revert_fn)(void *" ctx ", uint64_t " id ,
.BI "                                     char *" refusal ", size_t " size );
.PP
.BI "int  tui_histview_init(tui_histview *" h ", tui_histview_mode " mode ,
.BI "                       tui_histview_revert_fn " revert ", void *" ctx );
.BI "void tui_histview_free(tui_histview *" h );
.BI "void tui_histview_set_rows(tui_histview *" h ", const tui_histview_row *" rows ", int " n );
.BI "void tui_histview_set_failed(tui_histview *" h ", int " failed );
.BI "int  tui_histview_selected(const tui_histview *" h );
.BI "const char *tui_histview_notice(const tui_histview *" h );
.BI "int  tui_histview_modal(const tui_histview *" h );
.BI "tui_histview_state tui_histview_handle(tui_histview *" h ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_histview_render(tui_histview *" h ", tui_canvas " c );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The history view of policies/undo-model.md, shared by the terminal interfaces.
The program reads the recorded steps from its server, gives them with
.BR tui_histview_set_rows ()
and a callback that asks the server to revert one; the widget draws them in a
.BR tui_table (3)
(columns time, who, operation, thing, old value, new value and a note), scrolls
them with the common list keys and goes back with Esc, q and Backspace.
.PP
.I mode
is
.B TUI_HISTVIEW_OBJECT
(the history of one object) or
.B TUI_HISTVIEW_RECENT
(recent changes: a column "Object" is added from
.IR object ).
The strings of a row are not copied and must stay valid until the next
.BR tui_histview_set_rows ();
the selection is kept by step
.IR id .
The note column shows "reverts N" for a step with
.I reverts
set and "not revertable" for a step with
.I revertable
0; a step that is both shows "not revertable".
With no rows the view shows "no recorded changes";
.BR tui_histview_set_failed (h,\ 1)
shows "could not be read" instead.
.PP
.BR tui_histview_handle ()
returns
.B TUI_HISTVIEW_OPEN
(stay),
.B TUI_HISTVIEW_BACK
(Esc, q or Backspace),
.B TUI_HISTVIEW_QUIT
(ctrl-c) or
.B TUI_HISTVIEW_REVERTED
(the callback reverted the step: reload the rows).
The colon key opens the action menu with the entry "Revert" (its quick key comes from
the library's verb table, see
.BR tui_keytable_init (3));
Enter opens the same confirmation at once.
The confirmation names the step, the thing and what it will become, and No is
the default: Enter on it does nothing and the callback is not called.
On Yes the callback is called once with the step's id; it returns 0, or \-1 with
the server's words in
.IR refusal ,
which are shown in one line at the bottom
.RB ( tui_histview_notice ()).
A step marked not revertable shows the notice "step N is not revertable" and
opens no dialog.
The question mark opens the help, made from the widget's own key table.
.BR tui_histview_modal ()
is 1 while the menu, the confirmation or the help is open.
.BR tui_histview_render ()
draws everything into
.IR c ,
the dialogs centred on top; the table's colours are the table's
.RB ( tui_table_set_colors (3)
on the
.I table
member).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_table_init (3),
.BR tui_keytable_init (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
